  "body": "What happens: the LinuxCNC and Tormach posts write `G64 P0` when a blend or smoothing tolerance is under the written resolution. Lengths have 3 decimals in mm and 4 in inch. The blend tolerance option permits 0.001 mm, which is 0.00004 in, so an inch program writes `G64 P0`. A smoothing tolerance under about 0.0005 mm (mm) or 0.00127 mm (inch) does the same. LinuxCNC reads `G64 P0` as `G64` with no deviation limit.\n\nExpected: write the smallest positive value (`P0.001` mm, `P0.0001` in), or refuse by name. Never write `P0`.\n\nEvidence (upstream/main `f0bdc5109`):\n- `assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps:65` (min 0.001 mm), `:137-140` (`fu` rounding), `:396`, `:540`.\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:562` has the same code.\n- `crates/app/src/smoothing.rs:42-50` (finish = tolerance x 0.5, no floor).\n\nFound by the post audit against the LinuxCNC manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means: no tolerance in the allowed range writes `P0` in mm or inch, on both posts, and a test pins the smallest value.\n",
